{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>I am a ger and toshav among you.</b> It was the custom for them to have burial plots, each man for his ancestral house, and one burial field in which they would bury all the gerim. Now Abraham said to the children of Heth: I am a ger from another land and I did not inherit a burial house in this land from my fathers, and now I am a toshav among you, for I desire to dwell in this land. Therefore, give me a burial possession to be mine as an eternal holding, like one of you. And because he said \"give,\" they thought he was requesting it from them as a gift, and they answered him: You are not considered in our eyes as a ger and toshav, but you are a king — the Elohim has appointed you king over us, and we and our land are servants to you. Take any burial house you desire and bury your dead there, and it shall be yours as a burial possession forever, for no man among us will withhold it from you."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:20.700551314Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}